## item 15 [PAPER-NOTE — 2026-09-25] TOOLFUZZ BASELINE — report these in the paper
- **ToolFuzz's own false-discovery rate is 46% for correctness failures** (Milev et al.
  2025, Table 3: authors hand-checked every positive, 622 TP / 534 FP). Report it next
  to any ToolFuzz correctness count, and/or hand-check a sample of our ToolFuzz
  correctness positives the same way before comparing.
- Their "runtime detection has no false positives" holds for LangChain tools (exception
  = crash); MCP servers return errors as protocol replies -> we split ENV / REJECT /
  CRASH (eval/score_toolfuzz.py). Report ToolFuzz's own number AND the CRASH subset.
- ToolFuzz targets tool-DOCUMENTATION errors, not security (paper §3/§5.3) — positioning
  vs ToFu (implementation vs documented security contract).
- Its taint-guided fuzzer loses taint over MCP (server is a separate process) ->
  degrades to type-based Faker generation. State as a limitation of applying it to MCP.
- First campaign's ToolFuzz numbers are withdrawn ("2,030 discrepancies" = tests run;
  harness artifacts). Final config: gpt-4.1-mini, 1 correctness set x 3 prompts,
  1 runtime prompt per failing input, cap 40 calls/tool. Details:
  findings/baselines/toolfuzz_method_20260923.md.

